course: dictionary
lesson: 13255
title: Glazed: shiny or dull?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word glazed has more than one meaning, so the words around it are your best clues. «The baker brushed the buns with egg, and they came out glazed and golden.» Brushed with egg and golden tell you glazed means covered with a shiny coat.
explain: Now read this one: «Her eyes glazed over during the long, boring lesson.» Eyes cannot be covered with a coat here. The clue is long, boring lesson, so glazed means dull and blank, as if she had stopped paying attention.
explain: Glazed is the past form of glaze, so glaze, glazes and glazing belong to the same family. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Glaze means a shiny coating put on something.
fact: «Glazed» food is covered with a shiny coating, like a glazed doughnut or glazed ham.
fact: «Glazed» pottery has a hard, shiny, glassy coat baked on.
fact: A «double-glazed» window has two layers of glass.
fact: «Eyes glazed over» means the eyes look dull and blank, as if not paying attention.
exercise: «The baker glazed the buns with sugar and jam.» What does glazed mean here? | Cut into small pieces | Kept cold in a cupboard | *Covered with a shiny coating | Burnt black on the bottom
exercise: «Her eyes glazed over during the long, boring talk.» What does glazed suggest? | Wet with tears | Bright and full of joy | *Dull and not paying attention | Tightly closed
exercise: Which word is the past form of glaze? | glazes | glazing | *glazed | glaze
test: «Our kitchen has double-glazed windows, so the heat stays inside.» What does double-glazed mean? | *Has two layers of glass | Has two colours of paint | Has two doors | Is made of wood
test: «The clay pot was glazed and then baked in the kiln.» What does glazed mean here? | Left out in the rain | *Coated with a hard, shiny, glassy layer | Painted with a brush of water | Broken into little pieces
exam: Ella says glazed always means shiny. Which sentence shows that glazed can mean dull and blank? | «The window was double-glazed.» | «The ham was glazed with honey.» | *«His eyes glazed over and he stopped listening.» | «The pot was glazed blue.»
